<main style="max-width: 1000px; margin: 48px auto; font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; line-height: 1.5;">
  <h1><%= @credentials.fetch("name") %> created</h1>

  <% if @credential_env_path %>
    <p>
      Development credentials were saved locally to ignored files.
      The running Rails process also received the webhook secret, so you can install the App immediately.
    </p>
    <pre style="white-space: pre-wrap; background: #f6f8fa; padding: 16px; border-radius: 8px;">source <%= @credential_env_path %></pre>
  <% else %>
    <p>GitHub returned the App credentials. Save them before leaving this page.</p>
  <% end %>

  <h2>App identity</h2>
  <pre style="white-space: pre-wrap; background: #f6f8fa; padding: 16px; border-radius: 8px;">RUNDIFF_GITHUB_APP_ID=<%= @credentials.fetch("id") %>
RUNDIFF_GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=<%= @credentials.fetch("client_id") %>
RUNDIFF_GITHUB_WEBHOOK_SECRET=<%= @credentials.fetch("webhook_secret") %>
RUNDIFF_GITHUB_PRIVATE_KEY_PATH=<%= @private_key_path %></pre>

  <h2>Private key</h2>
  <% if @credential_env_path %>
    <p>Saved to <code><%= @private_key_path %></code> with mode 0600.</p>
  <% else %>
    <p>Save this exact PEM to <code><%= @private_key_path %></code> and chmod it to 600:</p>
  <% end %>
  <pre style="white-space: pre-wrap; background: #f6f8fa; padding: 16px; border-radius: 8px;"><%= @credentials.fetch("pem") %></pre>

  <h2>Next</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><a href="<%= @install_url %>">Install <%= @credentials.fetch("name") %></a> on <code>rundiff-hq/rundiff</code>.</li>
    <li>Select only the <code>rundiff-hq/rundiff</code> repository for the development installation.</li>
    <li>Watch the Rails log for verified <code>installation</code> and <code>pull_request</code> deliveries.</li>
    <li>For a future Rails process, run <code>source <%= @credential_env_path || "tmp/github-app/development.env" %></code> before starting the server.</li>
  </ol>

  <p><strong>Do not commit the PEM or secrets.</strong> The repository ignores <code>tmp/*</code> and <code>.env*</code>.</p>
</main>
